    <description>             This is an Andor 2kx2k CCD camera operating at -85 degrees Celsius. It has a GOS-calibrated shutter that permits highly accurate astrometry (typical residual less than +/-0.20) for              objects moving many hundreds of arcseconds per minute. The camera control computer is             synched once per minute wot a GPS coordinated Network Time Protocol server to account for             any hardware-induced errors.         </description>
